ossible NAT traversal; it does not identify the responsible process or establish benign intent.\n6. A signature match alone does not establish an intrusion. A UID fixture explanation needs a matching owned test receipt.\n\nExample: 15 allowed STUN alert records with no process or client receipt support possible NAT traversal, unknown process and unknown client result. They do not support \"15 successful connections.\"\n\n\n# Separate sensor action from client result\n\n1. Read the sensor action and client evidence as separate observations.\n2. Allowed leaves client success unknown unless independent result evidence supports it.\n3. Blocked describes that sensor event. It does not establish what the whole application did afterward.\n4. A process/socket receipt can support attribution when its time and tuple match. It does not prove communication success.\n5. A client result must match the exact time, tuple and attempt supplied by the evidence adapter.\n6. A successful retry does not rewrite the outcome of an earlier blocked attempt.\n7. Leave intent and complete UDP delivery unresolved when the evidence cannot establish them.\n\nExample: the sensor blocked attempt A, and a client receipt reports success for retry B. Preserve the block for A and scope success to B. Do not say the sensor block failed or every application request succeeded.\n\n\n# Choose a resolving read-only check\n\n1. Name the uncertainty before choosing the check.\n2. Specify the evidence needed, including event time, endpoint tuple or rule revision where relevant.\n3. For process identity, request a contemporaneous process/socket receipt.\n4. For client outcome, request a matching client or server result. A process list is insufficient.\n5. For changing activity, confirm collection coverage and the actual prior window before interpreting novelty.\n6. For a rule match, inspect the exact installed rule and relevant owned test receipt.\n7. Describe the possible resolving result, then leave the check proposed until a receipt is supplied.\n\nExample: inspecting the application running now does not prove it owned a past STUN socket. Request a receipt covering that event's time and tuple.\n\ndetailed thinking off<|role_end|><role>HUMAN</role>{\"coverage\":{\"current_retained_records\":5,\"omitted_groups\":0,\"prior_window_available\":true,\"retained_window_complete\":true,\"udp_delivery_complete\":false},\"fixed_context_notices\":[\"coverage_limits\",\"sensor_action_not_client_result\",\"rule_match_not_intrusion_proof\"],\"groups\":[{\"count\":1,\"fields\":{\"action\":\"blocked\",\"destination_alias\":\"D02-remote\",\"destination_port\":3478,\"gid\":1,\"protocol\":\"UDP\",\"rev\":8,\"severity\":1,\"sid\":1000001,\"signature\":\"Synthetic controlled block\",\"source_alias\":\"D02-client\",\"source_port\":43002},\"first_receipt_utc\":\"2026-10-07T10:02:00+00:00\",\"handle\":\"g1\",\"last_receipt_utc\":\"2026-10-07T10:02:00+00:00\"},{\"count\":4,\"fields\":{\"action\":\"allowed\",\"destination_alias\":\"D02-remote\",\"destination_port\":3478,\"gid\":1,\"protocol\":\"UDP\",\"rev\":8,\"severity\":3,\"sid\":2016149,\"signature\":\"Synthetic STUN match\",\"source_alias\":\"D02-client\",\"source_port\":43002},\"first_receipt_utc\":\"2026-10-07T10:02:01+00:00\",\"handle\":\"g2\",\"last_receipt_utc\":\"2026-10-07T10:02:04+00:00\"}],\"matched_receipts\":[],\"permitted_check_codes\":[\"compare_retained_window\",\"correlate_client_receipt\",\"correlate_process_receipt\",\"inspect_coverage\",\"inspect_rule\",\"none\"],\"permitted_context_codes\":[\"client_receipt_scoped_to_attempt\",\"comparison_incomplete\",\"coverage_limits\",\"possible_fixture_requires_receipt\",\"process_receipt_not_client_result\",\"rule_match_not_intrusion_proof\",\"sensor_action_not_client_result\",\"stun_process_unknown\",\"untrusted_log_text\"],\"unmatched_receipts\":[],\"untrusted_annotations\":[\"Constructed offline fixture, no captured network traffic.\"],\"useful_next_checks\":[\"correlate_client_rec